{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#449","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#449","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#449\",\"parent_revision\":\"1aba9ab80c5ad5ee39f9e1017b87656957c89614\",\"root_revision\":\"aa0c68f4e657272c3002219237e717b92e2f34fd5c5ac8581d695057bc231ba9\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nTasks that fail and are marked BLOCKED currently stay BLOCKED permanently. There is no automatic retry path \u2014 a human must manually reset the status to NOT STARTED or the task is abandoned for the session.\\n\\nSymphony's model: each failed worker records an attempt count; the orchestrator schedules a retry with exponential backoff (`min(10000 * 2^(attempt-1), max_retry_backoff_ms)`); on retry, the issue is re-fetched from the tracker \u2014 if it's no longer active, the claim is released instead of retrying.\\n\\n**Proposed behaviour:**\\n- Add `RetryCount` and `RetryAfter` fields to task metadata (YAML frontmatter and legacy markdown formats).\\n- When task_status_hook.py detects a SubagentStop with no COMPLETE marker, increment RetryCount and set RetryAfter = now + backoff(RetryCount).\\n- implementation_manager.py `ready-tasks` command: include tasks where status=BLOCKED, RetryCount < max_retries (default 3), and RetryAfter <= now.\\n- implement-feature passes `attempt=N` in the delegation prompt when RetryCount > 0.\\n- Max retries configurable; exhausted retries leave task BLOCKED with `max retries exceeded` note.\\n\\n**Acceptance criteria:**\\n- A task that fails is automatically retried up to 3 times with increasing delay.\\n- RetryCount and RetryAfter are visible in `implementation_manager.py status` output.\\n- After max retries, task stays BLOCKED permanently and is not re-dispatched.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: Retry with exponential backoff for BLOCKED tasks\\nDate: 2026-04-23\\nGoal: Add RetryCount + RetryAfter fields to task metadata and wire retry scheduling into task_status_hook.py and the ready-tasks command.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. task_status_hook.py SubagentStop handler | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py \u2014 detects COMPLETE absence\\n2. Task model fields for RetryCount + RetryAfter | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py \u2014 Task class; no retry fields currently\\n3. get_ready_tasks readiness logic | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py \u2014 checks status + dependencies\\n4. Backoff formula | AVAILABLE (documented) | min(10000 * 2^(attempt-1), max_retry_backoff_ms); default cap 5 min (from Symphony spec)\\n5. implement-feature delegation prompt modification | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md \u2014 add attempt=N to prompt when RetryCount > 0\\n6. Max retries and backoff cap configurability | DERIVABLE | default 3 retries, 5-min cap; env var or task-level override needs design\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 5\\nDERIVABLE count: 1\\nMISSING count: 0\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 complete implementation path defined; configurability mechanism is the only design decision.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **retry with exponential backoff for blocked tasks** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: OpenAI Symphony SPEC.md \u00a78 \u2014 failure-driven retry: delay = min(10000 * 2^(attempt-1), max_retry_backoff_ms); default cap 5 min\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `Task` model includes `retry_count: int = 0` and `retry_after: datetime | None = None` fields in `sam_schema/core/models.py`\\n- [ ] `task_status_hook.py` SubagentStop handler: when task ends without COMPLETE marker, increments `retry_count` and sets `retry_after = now + min(10000 * 2**(retry_count-1), 300000) ms`\\n- [ ] `get_ready_tasks` includes BLOCKED tasks where `retry_count < 3` (or configurable max) AND `retry_after <= now`\\n- [ ] After 3 failed retries, task stays BLOCKED permanently with `context_notes` entry `max retries exceeded after 3 attempts`\\n- [ ] `implement-feature` delegation prompt includes `attempt: N` when `retry_count > 0` so agent knows it's a retry\\n- [ ] `uv run sam status P{N}` output shows `retry_count` and `retry_after` for BLOCKED tasks with retries\\n- [ ] `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/` \u2014 zero errors on modified files\\n- [ ] Unit test: SubagentStop on BLOCKED task writes retry_count=1 and retry_after ~10s; second BLOCKED stop writes retry_count=2 and retry_after ~20s; third writes retry_count=3 with max-retries note, task not included in ready list\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 Task model (add retry_count, retry_after)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 SubagentStop handler (retry logic)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py` \u2014 get_ready_tasks (retry scheduling)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 delegation prompt (add attempt=N)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 document retry_count and retry_after fields\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/` \u2014 unit tests for retry logic\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an **implement-feature orchestrator handling a BLOCKED task**, I want **automatic retry with exponential backoff** so that **transient failures don't permanently stall a plan \u2014 a task gets 3 attempts before a human must intervene**.\\n\",\"digest\":\"39539d07e13d1d0c93eea48d6d04fca67b2aa5a758db2ee96e6f62c49f93c8e0\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg02lw\"}"}